            <ArticleTitle>Degradation of cardiac structural proteins induced by reperfusion in the infarcted myocardium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>195-202</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A combination of 2 h-occlusion and 22 h-reperfusion of the left circumflex coronary artery caused degradation of myosin heavy chain, alpha-actinin, troponin-I and myosin light chain 1 in the infarcted myocardial tissues in dogs. This degradation pattern of myocardial proteins differs from that observed in the dog with 24 h-occlusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
